{"id":"b7105664111bee987314c297a33165c9d9e9834655d58da9db9ed7ca5f3c7c92","lamport":1,"author":"scual.project@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-11-08T20:21:42.980896033Z","format_version":1,"kind":"set-field","payload":{"fields":{"description":"## Parent\n\nSub-issue of 215ee3.\n\n## What to build\n\nA property-based test proves the Sync invariants under scenarios nobody wrote by hand. At the library seam, two ticket stores share a bare remote in a tempdir. proptest (dev-dependency) generates random sequences of create, comment, tag, subissue, depends, delete, undelete and sync on either clone, with Race windows injected by interposing an edit-and-push on the other clone between a sync's pull and push. An in-memory model tracks expected state. After a final quiescent sync of both clones: every applied operation, comment and link is present on both; deleted tickets stay deleted on both; no parent/children or depends-on/blocks asymmetry; both clones project identical tickets. 32 cases by default, `PROPTEST_CASES` overrides. Failures shrink to a minimal sequence.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Test lives in the library crate, runs in `cargo test` under a few tens of seconds at 32 cases\n- [ ] Invariants: NoLostLocalOp (ops, comments, set members), NoResurrection, NoAsymmetry, Convergence\n- [ ] Race injection exercised in at least some generated cases\n- [ ] Seeding the pre-fix incident sequence by hand fails against the pre-fix code path (documented in the test as the motivating case)"}}}